# document_revision.p0t — SC40-A: imparare cambia cio' che il testo gia' letto significa.
#
# La proprieta' sotto prova non e' il replay. Il documento compare UNA volta;
# dopo, soltanto lezioni naturali. Superficie e span restano osservazioni
# immutabili, mentre gap/frame sono versioni dipendenti dalla KB corrente.

[mock live]
!set PARROT0_BASE=kb/core/base.p0
!set PARROT0_SESSION=
!set PARROT0_WORLD_FACTS=1
!set PARROT0_PROFILE=kb/profiles/agi.p0
!set PARROT0_LANG=en
!reset

[test sc40 baseline lezione revisione senza rilettura]
!timeout 120
# BASELINE: la procedura e' mappata ma `warm` non autorizza ancora un frame.
> read: https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK21154/ Before this the reaction requires a buffer. We then warm the tube. This repeats until the cycles reach forty.
<~ document unit(s)
!query claim_normalization_gap(document_a89aaeaeb2e06370_8b32e8d21149aa6b_unit_1_claim_0, no_reading)
!query method_executable(document_a89aaeaeb2e06370_8b32e8d21149aa6b, blocked(unbound_step))
!query! claim_frame(document_a89aaeaeb2e06370_8b32e8d21149aa6b_unit_1_claim_0, warm, authors, tube)
> was it described that the authors warm the tube?
< I recognize this as a described verification question, but I cannot normalize its proposition yet.

# LEZIONE NATURALE. Non c'e' un secondo `read:`: la lettura osservata viene
# ricalcolata dalla stessa fase pura e il metodo diventa eseguibile da solo.
> warm is a relation verb
< Learned: relation_verb(warm).
!query claim_frame(document_a89aaeaeb2e06370_8b32e8d21149aa6b_unit_1_claim_0, warm, authors, tube)
!query! claim_normalization_gap(document_a89aaeaeb2e06370_8b32e8d21149aa6b_unit_1_claim_0, no_reading)
!query method_executable(document_a89aaeaeb2e06370_8b32e8d21149aa6b, ready)
!query reading_depends_on($Reading, relation_verb(warm))
!query revision_effect(document_a89aaeaeb2e06370_8b32e8d21149aa6b_unit_1_claim_0, before($Old), after($New))
!query reading_stale($Old, superseded_by($New))
!query claim_reading_record(document_a89aaeaeb2e06370_8b32e8d21149aa6b_unit_1_claim_0, $Old, signature(gap(no_reading), proposition(none), extent(unknown)))
!query claim_reading_record(document_a89aaeaeb2e06370_8b32e8d21149aa6b_unit_1_claim_0, $New, signature(normalized(reported), proposition(frame(warm, roles(subject(authors), object(tube)))), extent(1, 1)))
# La nuova comprensione resta attribuita al documento: non diventa credenza.
!query claim_status(document_a89aaeaeb2e06370_8b32e8d21149aa6b_unit_1_claim_0, described)
!query claim_commitment(document_a89aaeaeb2e06370_8b32e8d21149aa6b_unit_1_claim_0, attributed_only)
!query! warm(authors, tube)
!query! holds_in(world, proposition(frame(warm, roles(subject(authors), object(tube)))))
> was it described that the authors warm the tube?
< Yes - that claim is reported as described (from https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK21154/).

[test sc40 ablation e riapprendimento rivedono lo stesso testo]
!timeout 120
# ABLATION PARLATA: il frame corrente perde la propria base e lo stesso pass
# produce un nuovo gap. Superficie, fonte e status non vengono cancellati.
> forget that warm is a relation verb
<~ warm
!query! relation_verb(warm)
!query! claim_frame(document_a89aaeaeb2e06370_8b32e8d21149aa6b_unit_1_claim_0, warm, authors, tube)
!query claim_normalization_gap(document_a89aaeaeb2e06370_8b32e8d21149aa6b_unit_1_claim_0, no_reading)
!query method_executable(document_a89aaeaeb2e06370_8b32e8d21149aa6b, blocked(unbound_step))
!query claim_surface(document_a89aaeaeb2e06370_8b32e8d21149aa6b_unit_1_claim_0, "warm the tube")
!query claim_status(document_a89aaeaeb2e06370_8b32e8d21149aa6b_unit_1_claim_0, described)
!query reading_stale($Reading, lost_dependency(relation_verb(warm)))
> was it described that the authors warm the tube?
< I recognize this as a described verification question, but I cannot normalize its proposition yet.

# RETEACH, ancora senza rilettura. Due turni estranei misurano ritenzione e
# l'idempotenza del pass: la comprensione non dipende dall'ultimo turno.
> warm is a relation verb
< Learned: relation_verb(warm).
!query claim_frame(document_a89aaeaeb2e06370_8b32e8d21149aa6b_unit_1_claim_0, warm, authors, tube)
!query method_executable(document_a89aaeaeb2e06370_8b32e8d21149aa6b, ready)
> a robin is a bird
<~ Learned
> Is a robin a bird?
< Yes.
!query claim_frame(document_a89aaeaeb2e06370_8b32e8d21149aa6b_unit_1_claim_0, warm, authors, tube)
!query method_executable(document_a89aaeaeb2e06370_8b32e8d21149aa6b, ready)

[test sc40 transfer at 3 su letteratura scientifica]
!timeout 180
!reset
# Tre predicati, generi e fonti distinti partono da un residuo e cambiano con
# una lezione lessicale one-shot, senza replay del documento.
> read: https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20230015804 The data show that the impact altered the orbit.
<~ reported claim(s)
!query claim_normalization_gap($Claim, no_reading)
> altered is a relation verb
< Learned: relation_verb(altered).
!query claim_frame($Claim, altered, impact, orbit)
!query reading_depends_on($Reading, relation_verb(altered))
!query! altered(impact, orbit)

> read: https://gmd.copernicus.org/articles/13/1959/2020/ The simulations show that the scheme perturbs the radiation field.
<~ reported claim(s)
!query claim_normalization_gap($Claim, no_reading)
> perturbs is a relation verb
< Learned: relation_verb(perturbs).
!query claim_frame($Claim, perturbs, scheme, radiation_field)
!query reading_depends_on($Reading, relation_verb(perturbs))
!query! perturbs(scheme, radiation_field)

> read: https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC10589119/ The evidence shows that confounding distorts the association.
<~ reported claim(s)
!query claim_normalization_gap($Claim, no_reading)
> distorts is a relation verb
< Learned: relation_verb(distorts).
!query claim_frame($Claim, distorts, confounding, association)
!query reading_depends_on($Reading, relation_verb(distorts))
!query! distorts(confounding, association)

# CONTRASTO: imparare un quarto verbo non inventa letture con quel predicato
# per testi che non lo contengono.
> catalyzes is a relation verb
< Learned: relation_verb(catalyzes).
!query! claim_frame($Claim, catalyzes, $Subject, $Object)
